  "comparisonNotes": [
    "Metrics are pooled over all frames of the split (micro-averaged cell counts).",
    "Ridge is evaluated on its per-frame output (no temporal smoothing) at 0.5, its validation-chosen operating point.",
    "rtiObservedValTuned applies a threshold chosen on the validation scenes, so both models get an operating point tuned on identical data.",
    "rti-bayes is the engine output of the same pipeline runs: per-voxel occupancy after the default EMA (0.5) and 3x3x3 box filter at 0.25 m voxels, projected to 0.5 m cells by max over z and over the 2x2 voxel columns of each cell.",
    "rtiObserved* takes the max over voxels with posterior variance ratio <= 0.95 only. rti-bayes reports 0.5 ('unknown') for unobserved voxels, which include the entire bottom and top voxel layers here, so the all-voxel projection (rtiAllVoxelsT05) marks every cell occupied at threshold 0.5.",
    "rtiObservedT06 uses the engine's default occupancyThreshold (0.6)."
  ],
